PL11's change to the Makefile, for the owner (the Makefile is protected; the slice does not edit it).

What it does: the `licence-check` target already runs `tools.licence_check` on its first line, and that now
includes the register leg (weights, map data, fonts and base images held to spec/LICENCE_REGISTER.yaml), so the
leg needs no new line. What the target lacked is the Python tests under tests/licence_check/ (test_register.py
and the files beside it), which only ci.yml's licence-check job ran. This adds them, as ci.yml's job does.

Apply from the repository root: git apply OspreyFlow_Build/process/lanes/v062/PL11_MAKEFILE.diff

--- a/OspreyFlow_Build/Makefile
+++ b/OspreyFlow_Build/Makefile
@@ -91,8 +91,9 @@
 licence-check:
 	$(IN_CORE) $(TOOLS) $(PY) -m tools.licence_check
 	$(IN_CORE) node $(BUILD)/tools/licence_check.mjs
+	$(IN_CORE) $(PYTEST) $(BUILD)/tests/licence_check
 	$(IN_CORE) node --test $(BUILD)/tests/licence_check/*.test.mjs
-	@echo "licence-check: tests/licence_check/test_gpl_rejection.py and test_licence_check_mjs.test.mjs hold the proof"
+	@echo "licence-check: tests/licence_check/test_gpl_rejection.py and test_licence_check_mjs.test.mjs hold the proof; test_register.py holds it for the register leg (weights, map data, fonts, base images), which the first line above runs"
 
